{"id":571,"flavor":[{"games":["Legends: Arceus"],"text":"With its disheveled white fur, it looks like an embodiment of death. Heedless of its own safety, Zoroark attacks its nemeses with a bitter energy so intense, it lacerates Zoroark's own body."},{"games":["Shield"],"text":"Seeking to ease the burden of their solitude, lonely Trainers tell Zoroark to show illusions to them."},{"games":["Sword"],"text":"This Pokémon cares deeply about others of its kind, and it will conjure terrifying illusions to keep its den and pack safe."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"If it thinks humans are going to discover its den, Zoroark shows them visions that make them wander around in the woods."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"It doesn’t just transform itself—it also has the power to make hundreds of people see its illusions."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Y","Black"],"text":"Bonds between these Pokémon are very strong. It protects the safety of its pack by tricking its opponents."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","X","White"],"text":"Each has the ability to fool a large group of people simultaneously. They protect their lair with illusory scenery."},{"games":["White 2","Black 2"],"text":"Stories say those who tried to catch Zoroark were trapped in an illusion and punished."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Illusion","hidden":false,"description":"The Pokémon fools opponents by entering battle disguised as the last Pokémon in its Trainer's party."}],"eggGroups":["Field"],"genderRate":1,"hatchCounter":20,"baseHappiness":70,"growthRate":"medium slow","habitat":null,"color":"Gray","shape":"Upright","evolution":{"id":570,"name":"Zorua","condition":null,"children":[{"id":571,"name":"Zoroark","condition":"Lv. 30","children":[]}]},"moves":{"game":"Scarlet / Violet","level":[[0,400],[1,10],[1,43],[1,259],[1,369],[1,468],[12,154],[20,269],[24,282],[28,313],[34,97],[40,286],[46,539],[52,417],[58,492]],"machine":[332,97,34,280,807,347,109,242,399,91,203,263,313,53,374,411,492,416,447,270,506,63,304,286,282,808,6